From f66d6e4d78d8f25da5fc4b0cad7d294ef0f57fe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Tsukerman <miketsukerman@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:04:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] imx95: AOM-5521 on SOM-DB2510 board support

- Read the Ethernet MAC addresses from the module's SPI NOR.
- Pulse SW_RESET_OUT# instead of enabling the EVK M.2 regulator.
- Describe the module's quad W25Q64JW SPI NOR.
- Add USB OTG VBUS regulator, ID extcon and the PCA6416 at 0x21.
- Add imx95-aom5521-db2510-u-boot.dtsi describing the module's
  Ethernet: two RTL8211FSI on RGMII (ENET1 -> PHY@3 -> GBE1,
  ENET2 -> PHY@1 -> GBE0), shared EMDIO, no switchable PHY supply and
  no software PHY reset, enetc_port2 disabled.
- Disable the EVK-only I2C GPIO expanders, CAN and video pipeline,
  and drop the EVK PHY reset / AQR-MAC regulator handling from
  netc_init().
- Set the DDR size to 8 GiB.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific]
